# XSH thrd_sleep()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only lower bounds on the elapsed time are checked (TIME_UTC); the
# upper end is a hang guard. The remaining time is checked against what
# the page defines: requested minus time actually slept.

assertion  XSH.thrd_sleep.001
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_sleep() for 200 ms returns 0 and the TIME_UTC clock has
           advanced by at least 200 ms; a zero duration returns 0, and so
           does a completed sleep with a non-null remaining.
test       t/001-elapsed.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_sleep.002
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_sleep(5 s) interrupted by a caught signal (SIGUSR1, no
           SA_RESTART) returns -1 with errno EINTR; the remaining time is
           greater than zero and at most 5 s, and the time slept plus the
           remaining time is at least the 5 s requested.
test       t/002-interrupted.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_sleep.003
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With duration and remaining pointing to the same object, an
           interrupted thrd_sleep() returns -1 (EINTR) and leaves the
           remaining time in it: more than zero, at most 5 s, and with the
           time slept at least the 5 s requested.
test       t/003-same-object.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_sleep.004
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#ERRORS
anchor     functions/thrd_sleep.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_sleep() with tv_nsec equal to 1000000000, and with tv_nsec
           equal to -1, returns a negative value and sets errno to EINVAL.
test       t/004-einval.c
